Proposed (53.2s): Use this skill when someone wants to map out, document, or visualize how a software system is built — its users, systems, services/containers, components, and how they connect — as a C4 model written in Structurizr DSL (workspace.dsl). This covers creating or editing a .dsl workspace; producing system-context, container, component, deployment, dynamic, or system-landscape views; and modeling how microservices fit together — even if they never name "Structurizr" or "C4". It also covers pulling existing decision records (ADRs from doc/adr or similar) INTO that architecture documentation, so the C4 views or workspace surface the related decisions — i.e. wiring ADRs into the diagrams, not writing the decisions. Skip it for cloud pictures drawn with real vendor service icons (AWS EC2/RDS/S3 boxes, draw.io / diagrams.net art), for sequence or flow diagrams, and for writing, revising, or superseding the ADR content itself.

